{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwcDHLkcqZVqqRZCTRsr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard or confirmed the rule has run, so I can't say whether the panels render or the rule evaluates cleanly.\n\n**Data:** The Kibana Sample Data Logs view has web-access fields: `timestamp`, `response` (the status code, stored as text), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `geo.src`/`geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `url` and `host`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-b32cdafa Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Responses by status code\n- Average bytes by extension\n\nIt is at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-b32cdafa-web-logs-overview-0a872544baee.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-b32cdafa 5xx spike\" (ID `3c85ce2c-4e34-457a-92e7-313fb13ff396`) runs every minute. It counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` whose `response.keyword` matches `5xx` over a 5-minute window, and fires when that count is above 10. I created it without any notification action, so it will show as active in Kibana but won't send anything.\n\nThe sample data's timestamps are shifted to the time it was loaded, so unless it is refreshed the rule may see few or no recent 5xx documents."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":161,"cache_read_input_tokens":20287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":161},"output_tokens":471,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"6c7a64c2-d54e-4c4c-a462-b186c5b8a31a","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:09:17.866Z","request_id":"req_011CfwcDH3diKoHmAWWfpCqA"}
